{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01842",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 9.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "Hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second. What would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.1,
      "end_seconds": 16.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "yeah, it's a little breathlessness. I don't know what's causing it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.27,
      "end_seconds": 21.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.34,
      "end_seconds": 29.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, it's been like this since Monday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.85,
      "end_seconds": 33.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "hm, okay is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.36,
      "end_seconds": 38.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.79,
      "end_seconds": 42.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Have you tried anything for it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.12,
      "end_seconds": 47.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Erm, resting helps a a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.94,
      "end_seconds": 51.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Right, is it worse at certain times?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.77,
      "end_seconds": 57.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "yes, stairs. That makes it worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.58,
      "end_seconds": 62.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.82,
      "end_seconds": 83.51,
      "duration_seconds": 19.69,
      "text": "Ah, when it starts I tend to get tiredness as well. Erm, you know, I've been feeling nervous about exertion too, for about a week. The tiredness? That's been for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.23,
      "end_seconds": 94.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "let me check a few things any palpitations, fainting or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.22,
      "end_seconds": 99.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "no palpitations, fainting or leg swelling, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.06,
      "end_seconds": 103.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.65,
      "end_seconds": 107.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.79,
      "end_seconds": 126.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.69,
      "end_seconds": 140.49,
      "duration_seconds": 13.8,
      "text": "mm, I'm on lisinopril, 10 milligrams, once a day for my pressure. Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day for my heart"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.42,
      "end_seconds": 143.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.49,
      "end_seconds": 152.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "I, I had a meniscus repair on my knee four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.21,
      "end_seconds": 157.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.76,
      "end_seconds": 166.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "I, I have high blood pressure, for about a year"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.71,
      "end_seconds": 168.66,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.19,
      "end_seconds": 176.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Let me think, I have heart disease, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.8,
      "end_seconds": 185.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Yes, heart disease is known to us, good to have that clear. Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.85,
      "end_seconds": 196.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "I swim twice a week. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.14,
      "end_seconds": 204.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.28,
      "end_seconds": 208.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "not to my knowledge, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.23,
      "end_seconds": 212.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.55,
      "end_seconds": 224.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.67,
      "end_seconds": 250.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 126 over 80, saturation 99 percent, pulse 76, temp 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.17,
      "end_seconds": 256.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.13,
      "end_seconds": 267.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.28,
      "end_seconds": 270.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.76,
      "end_seconds": 286.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "your heart rate and rhythm are regular and the breastbone wound has healed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.69,
      "end_seconds": 292.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.84,
      "end_seconds": 335.63,
      "duration_seconds": 24.79,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. The most likely explanation is recovering well after a heart attack. I'd like to arrange a cholesterol test for secondary prevention. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'll request an ECG, it'll help with post heart attack review. Start the rehabilitation classes and build up walking gradually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.22,
      "end_seconds": 347.33,
      "duration_seconds": 11.11,
      "text": "Okay, go on. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. I'll also refer you to the cardiac rehabilitation team."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.29,
      "end_seconds": 349.99,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.7,
      "end_seconds": 356.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "If the the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.75,
      "end_seconds": 359.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "I'll remember that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.3,
      "end_seconds": 366.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Book a review in three months. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.07,
      "end_seconds": 371.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.17,
      "end_seconds": 373.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}